<title>USA: Albany Cty Airport, NY, bonds get final OK - paper.</title>
<headline>Albany Cty Airport, NY, bonds get final OK - paper.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Albany County Airport, N.Y., got final approval for a $100 million bond sale to pay for improvements when the county comptroller raised no objection at an Authority meeting Monday, Albany Times Union reported Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bonds, which will be sold through negotiation in a syndicate headed by Lehman Brothers, are expected to be come to market between Feb 13 and 20.</p>
<p>Local residents will get the benefit of a pre-sale order period, according to an agreement made last week, which also reduced the offerings' maturity to 27 years from 30 years.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
